 "final_text": "**Submitted.** One number Treasury can defend:\n\n| Field | Amount | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| ERP open balance | $94,749.19 | 3 open, undisputed invoices on SYNCUS-0002 \"Adventure Works Cycles\" |\n| Subsidiary net balance | $19,050.00 | Direct-channel books (BC-114), $22,200 open less $3,150 unapplied credit memo |\n| **Combined exposure** | **$113,799.19** | Sum across both systems |\n\nThe key risk this avoided: the ERP has 36 similarly-named \"Adventure Works *\" customers (South, Global, Pro, Premium, etc.) that aren't the same counterparty \u2014 the Books ledger's explicit `ERP ref: SYNCUS-0002` note was the only reliable link tying the direct-channel subsidiary balance to the correct ERP entity. I also netted out the $3,150 unapplied credit memo rather than reporting the gross $22,200, since QBO-style reports don't net credits automatically and that would have overstated real exposure.",
